From 51e2256d447755f932ae001799a7a2f160797c41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:16:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] vulkan: fixed GPU mode runs small-M weight matmuls on
 the host when the bits match

Batched embedding under MoltenVK: a single short text through embed_many was ~20% slower
than per-text (58.6 vs 49.0 ms, macos-15): the fixed Gpu mode sends every weight matmul to
the GPU, one submit + wait (~0.8 ms) each, where the Auto mode keeps small ones on the host.

On host-shared memory, F32 weight matmuls with 2..=CANDLE_VULKAN_HOST_SMALL_M rows (default
32) now run on the host, but only for the weight shapes whose host result is bit-identical to
the GPU kernel's (checked once per device and shape on 16 rows of the real weight; Apple
Silicon gives the same digest on CPU, MoltenVK and Metal). Rows therefore still do not depend
on the batch they are in; a shape that differs stays on the GPU. Logged as [VK-HOST-SMALL-M].

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GcxyAs2y3NUizfXh9YWmxx
